{
  "_comment": "Configurable, deliberately short. This list exists for ONE job: catching a bot caption that jokes about WHO the people in the photo are instead of WHAT is happening. It is not a profanity filter, it does not enumerate slurs, and it never runs on a human's caption. Edit this file to tune it; src/shared/caption-guard.ts reads it and agent/lib.mjs reads the same file, so the two cannot drift.",
  "_comment_colours": "Colour words (black / white / brown) are NOT in `descriptors`. They are ordinary English adjectives about objects (black cat, white wine, black tie, Black Friday, black and white photo) far more often than they are labels on a person, so they only count as a label when the very next word names a person. That is why they appear below as explicit two-word phrases instead.",
